        "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnolia_denudata",
        "description": "Magnolia denudata, the lilytree or Yulan magnolia (simplified Chinese: \\u7389\\u5170\\u82b1; traditional Chinese: \\u7389\\u862d\\u82b1; pinyin: y\\u00f9l\\u00e1nhu\\u0101; lit. 'jade orchid/lily'), is native to central and eastern China. It has been cultivated in Chinese Buddhist temple gardens since 600 AD. Its flowers were regarded as a symbol of purity in the Tang dynasty and it was planted in the grounds of the emperor's palace. It is the official city flower of Shanghai."
